WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Step 1 of 6. Seat the column in the base. Place the base casting on a stable bench, then lower the column into the base socket. Align it carefully and seat it until the dowel engages. If needed, use light taps through a wood block to bring the column fully home without forcing the fit. Warning: Do not force the fit..

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Step 2 of 6. Install base-to-column hardware. With the column seated, install the two M10 bolts with lock washers up through the base into the column. Start both fasteners and bring them to finger-tight only so the assembly can still self-align during the travel check later. Warning: WARNING: Do not apply final torque until ram travel is verified in step 5..

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Step 3 of 6. Slide the ram into the column. Prepare the ram by wiping the rack clean and applying a thin film of machine oil to the rack teeth. Then lower the ram into the top of the column and continue until the rack becomes visible in the pinion window.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:32.000
Step 4 of 6. Mesh the pinion and fit the handle. Insert the pinion shaft through the column boss so its teeth engage the ram rack. Once the mesh is established, fit the handle assembly onto the pinion square and secure it using the specified hex-key-retained connection.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Step 5 of 6. Verify travel and torque the base bolts. Cycle the handle to move the ram through its full travel and confirm the motion is smooth with no binding. After the travel check passes, tighten both base-to-column bolts to final torque. Warning: WARNING: Keep fingers clear of the ram path while cycling..

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Step 6 of 6. Fit the rack guard. Place the rack guard over the pinion window, align the mounting holes, and install the four socket cap screws. Tighten the screws evenly, then torque all four to specification.
